    <string name="about_title">Privacy and about</string>
    <string name="about_body">LocalSpend stores every transaction in a database on this device only. The app uses the internet only to look up exchange rates (just two currency codes and a date are sent, and you can turn it off in Settings), so your financial data never leaves the device, and Android backup is switched off.\n\nSMS messages are read on the device to extract the amount, merchant, date and type. The complete original message is kept with its transaction so you can always check what was extracted (menu → SMS messages). You can switch this off or delete the stored messages in Settings.\n\nEach transaction keeps its own currency (dollars or rupees), and payments in other currencies are converted into your main currency at the rate of the day they happened.\n\nCategories are yours to change: rename them, recolour them, add your own, give them keywords and monthly budgets. Correct any transaction\'s category and LocalSpend remembers it for that merchant.\n\nInsights are calculated on the device and are never used for advertising.</string>
